From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:19:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wayland/color-management: Publish descriptions on exact
 identity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The output's description and a surface's preferred description were
republished only when the new color state differed by
clutter_color_state_equals(), which treats luminances within 10% as
equal, while the color device, the renderer and the mapping predicate
use exact identity. A reference luminance factor change under 10%, such
as 0.80 to 0.87 (reference white 162 to 177 cd/m²), changed the
rendering without being published, so a client following the published
description declared the old reference white and was mapped again.

Compare with clutter_color_state_identical(), pointer equality included,
next to the target comparison, as the renderer does.

A new separate test case, /wayland/published/reference-factor, changes
the factor within 10% and checks, at the published-record level, that
the description is republished with the new reference white, and that
a client copying the published reference white and target luminance is
not mapped and keeps direct scanout after each change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLZiLBYev72J1s4D37L7Bi
---
 src/tests/meson.build                         |   4 +-
 src/tests/wayland-color-management-test.c     | 101 +++++++++++++++++
 .../wayland-test-clients/color-management.c   | 105 ++++++++++++++++++
 src/wayland/meta-wayland-color-management.c   |  11 +-
 4 files changed, 217 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

